{
  "contract": "photo-cards",
  "version": 2,
  "minAppBuild": 119,
  "notes": [
    "Photo cards v1 (2026-09-26): NO AI anywhere. The photo is cleaned up on the server with ffmpeg (EXIF rotate, per-channel auto levels / colour-cast and fade correction, gentle denoise, unsharp, slight saturation lift); the card is drawn on the phone from the spec with bundled fonts and vector designs.",
    "REST JSON is camelCase; tool arguments are snake_case; a deviceAction's top-level keys are snake_case and the poster/photo objects inside it use the REST shape.",
    "Errors are {error: code, message} plus extra fields named per error (need, poster).",
    "Text is never truncated, re-cased, translated or corrected: over a limit the server answers 422 {error:'need'} and the app asks to shorten.",
    "words(spec) — examples.words — is exactly what the card prints, top to bottom; the 'from' line is printed as given (the app may add a decorative dash, never words).",
    "Non-English cards keep the heading from the table and show the age as a numeral beside it (examples.words_ml has it as its own line).",
    "A photo's status is always 'ready' in v1 and variants are ['original','enhanced'] (just ['original'] when the server has no ffmpeg). reason is 'off' (AI repair not switched on) or 'not_requested' (ai=false).",
    "POST /posters/photos/:id/restore always answers 503 {error:'off', message:'Photo repair is not switched on yet.'} in v1.",
    "The signature never reaches the server: spec.signature is only on/off; the strokes stay in the phone's secure storage under 'poster.signature.v1'.",
    "spec.photoColour ('keep'|'bw'|'sepia', default 'keep') is the colour of the CARD's photo: change it with PATCH {change:{photoColour}} — a versioned edit in the undo history. Draw the card from GET /posters/photos/:id/file?v=enhanced&colour=<spec.photoColour> (each colour is its own URL). POST /posters/photos/:id/colour is only for a photo shown on its own (the improve-old-photo screen); it no longer changes any card.",
    "A photo arriving on a card (upload with posterId, create with photoId, PATCH change.photoId) brings its own colour (photo.colour) into spec.photoColour unless the change names one.",
    "DELETE /posters/photos/:id removes one working photo for good: it is taken off every card that shows it (spec.photoUse 'none', the words stay) and out of their undo history; the answer lists the cards that changed (posterIds) — refetch them. DELETE /posters/consent does that for every working photo and answers {accepted:false, photosRemoved}.",
    "Uploads: 413 too_large is either over 18 MB or too many pixels to open (over 24 MP after a JPEG's reduced decode); 415 unsupported_type is bytes that are not a JPEG/PNG/WebP or that do not decode. The type is read from the bytes, not the declared mime.",
    "photo_shown carries the photo's id ({photo_id}) so the model can keep it (improve_old_photo {photo_id, keep}) or put it on a card (make_greeting_poster {photo_id})."
  ],
  "limits": {
    "headline": 60,
    "name": 60,
    "message": 300,
    "from": 80,
    "date": 40,
    "forWhom": 40,
    "messageMaxNewlines": 4,
